[head=1]A note on medibots in Brigmed:[/head]

Medibots dispense [color=#00e5ff]TRICORDRAZINE[/color] under 50 damage and [color=#731024]INAPROVALINE[/color]  in [color=red]CRITICAL[/color] patients both useful in isolation. The issue is [color=#3a1d8a]DYLOVINE[/color].

When a patient has poison damage, I need [color=#3a1d8a]DYLOVINE[/color] to treat it. [color=#3a1d8a]DYLOVINE[/color] and [color=#731024]INAPROVALINE[/color] react into [color=#00e5ff]TRICORDRAZINE[/color], which does not treat poison. On a critical patient with active poison damage, a medibot's [color=#731024]INAPROVALINE[/color] will neutralize the [color=#3a1d8a]DYLOVINE[/color] before it can work and poison damage cannot be treated topically, so we are now racing against a clock we didn't need to start.

I would rather spend the extra seconds dosing manually than untangle that mid-emergency. Medibots belong in Medbay or low-risk areas.

Not here.

- Ciro.V.M.
